BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:165013@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20260915T112201Z
DTSTART:20261001T160000Z
DTEND:20261001T170000Z
SUMMARY:ISO-NE Longer-Term Transmission Planning & Procurement Public Webinar
LOCATION:Microsoft Teams
DESCRIPTION:ISO New England (ISO-NE) will host a virtual public webinar to provide an overview of the longer-term transmission planning (LTTP) process and the first LTTP procurement on Oct. 1 from 12:00 – 1:00 pm. \n\nIn 2025\, at the direction of the New England States Committee on Electricity (NESCOE)\, ISO New England issued a request for proposals (RFP) aimed at addressing longer-term transmission needs in the region identified in connection with the 2050 Transmission Study. In August\, after several months of evaluation and stakeholder discussions\, ISO selected a preferred solution to upgrade the transmission system between northern Maine\, where land-based wind generation is expected to increase\, and more populous regions of southern New England\, where demand for electricity is highest. The ISO will be providing updates on next steps in the process\, as appropriate\, through the Planning Advisory Committee.\n\nContent will be based on publicly available information and is intended for a general audience. This webinar will build on information shared at an earlier webinar on the 2050 Transmission Study\, the ISO’s first longer-term transmission study. There will be time for questions\, and a recording will be posted following the event.\n\nAdd to My Calendar\n\nRegistration is not required. This event will be held virtually via Teams:\n\nJoin: https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/263535212213275?p=HKrHnYcX4bvoh6LOdv\n\nMeeting ID: 263 535 212 213 275\n\nPasscode: yd6NE6dB\nContact: Melissa Winne (mwinne@iso-ne.com )\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165013
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165013
END:VEVENT
